                "pass_filenames": false,
                "_comment": "EPIC-ACTreeSplit: Enforces ACS-100c-1 hard caps (>7 L1s per L0, >5 L2s per L1) and emits ACS-100c-2 sparse advisory (<3 children). Blocks commits that push a parent over its child limit. Fail-open on subprocess/YAML errors. Load ac-tree-split skill to resolve violations."
            },
            {
                "id": "check-ac-governance",
                "name": "Check AC Governance (ACS-400 write-lock for requirement-defining fields)",
                "entry": "python {{config.output_root}}/scripts/commit_guardian/run_hook.py {{config.output_root}}/scripts/commit_guardian/check_ac_governance.py",
                "language": "system",
                "files": "^docs/acceptance-criteria/.*\\.yaml$",
                "stages": [
                    "pre-commit"
                ],
                "pass_filenames": false,
                "_comment": "ACS-400: Blocks commits where an implementation agent modifies protected fields (criteria, title, req_status, depends_on) in AC YAML files. Only authorized requirement authors (product-owner-v3, business-analyst-v3, it-po-v3) and human users may write protected fields. Fail-open: exits 0 on any unexpected error."
            },
            {
                "id": "check-ac-parent-covered-by",
                "name": "Check AC Parent covered_by Back-Link (ACS-100i-2)",
                "entry": "python {{config.output_root}}/scripts/commit_guardian/run_hook.py {{config.output_root}}/scripts/commit_guardian/check_ac_parent_covered_by.py",
                "language": "system",
                "files": "^docs/acceptance-criteria/.*\\.yaml$",
                "stages": [
                    "pre-commit"
                ],
                "pass_filenames": false,
                "_comment": "ACS-100i-2: Blocks commits where a staged child AC file's parent AC does not include the child ID in its covered_by field. Derives the parent ID using derive_parent_id() from scripts/ac_store/ac_parent_id.py. Fail-open on parse errors or missing parent files."
            },
            {
                "id": "check-ac-circular-deps",
                "name": "Check AC Circular depends_on Chains (ACS-500e-1-i)",
                "entry": "python {{config.output_root}}/scripts/commit_guardian/run_hook.py {{config.output_root}}/scripts/commit_guardian/check_ac_circular_deps.py",
                "language": "system",
                "files": "^docs/acceptance-criteria/.*\\.yaml$",
                "stages": [
                    "pre-commit"
                ],
                "pass_filenames": false,
                "_comment": "ACS-500e-1-i: Blocks commits when a staged AC YAML file's depends_on field would create a circular dependency chain. Builds the full depends_on graph from the AC store (overlaying staged changes), runs DFS cycle detection, and reports the full cycle path (e.g. 'Circular dependency detected: PTN-010 -> PTN-020 -> PTN-010'). Fail-open on unexpected errors."
            },
            {
                "id": "check-ac-pattern-refs",
                "name": "Check AC implements_pattern References (ACS-500a-3 / ACS-500d-1-i)",
                "entry": "python {{config.output_root}}/scripts/commit_guardian/run_hook.py {{config.output_root}}/scripts/commit_guardian/check_ac_pattern_refs.py",
